# GitHub language stats.
#
# This is a Zig project: the engine is src/ and shim/. Everything under spike/
# is apparatus, and most of it is a record rather than code — the sealed blind
# campaigns, the assisted cohorts, and the dormant pre-campaign spikes are
# evidence for claims made in PRD.md and DESIGN.md. They are never edited
# (blind-hunt through blind-hunt3 have taken no commit since 2026-08-14), and
# counting them made Shell the repository's largest language at 52%, ahead of
# the engine it exists to test.
#
# The rule used to run the other way: a directory counted as code until someone
# remembered to register it here when its campaign closed. It was missed on
# every closure it ever faced — cohort 4, then spike/macos-oracle/ (#181), then
# spike/scout-model-comparison/ (#221) — because nothing reads this file at the
# moment a record closes, which is by definition the moment attention leaves.
# The direction is inverted so that there is no closing moment to notice: a
# record is documentation from the day its directory is created.
#
#   spike/**       documentation.
#   spike/*        code. The maintained harness lives at the top level:
#                  acceptance.sh, mcp-acceptance.sh, campaign-driver.sh,
#                  rehearse-campaign.sh, the toy builders and the rest are
#                  shell that is actually maintained, and hiding them would
#                  overstate how much of this repository is Zig.
#   spike/toys/**  code. The only live directory: the planted-bug toys are
#                  compiled by ci.yml and by `sideeye demo`.
#
# Position carries the meaning, so neither a new record directory nor a new
# top-level script needs a line here. A new *live directory* still does — that
# is the one misclassification this direction can produce, and it is the safer
# one: it understates Shell rather than counting a frozen transcript as code,
# and it happens while someone is working in that directory rather than as they
# walk away from it. docs/adr/0021 records why that trade was taken.
#
# spike/check-gitattributes.sh holds this: every tracked file under spike/ must
# resolve to set or unset — never unspecified — and both directions above are
# checked over every file rather than a sample.

spike/**        linguist-documentation
spike/*        -linguist-documentation
spike/toys/**  -linguist-documentation
spike/lib/**   -linguist-documentation
